    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change moves date-derived values to a **fiscal-year basis** (fiscal year starts 1 July, identified by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 the Australian convention this app already follows via NSW/VIC/QLD regions, +61 phone numbers, and Australian holidays).\n\n**New `FiscalYear` utility** (`model/FiscalYear.java`) \u2014 a single-responsibility class holding all fiscal-year math, so the logic is reused rather than duplicated across the three call sites and `Owner` doesn't become a catch-all:\n- `endingYear(date)` \u2014 the calendar year the fiscal year ends in (July onward \u2192 next year).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 `'FY<YY>'`.\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years elapsed (1 July boundaries crossed).\n\n**`Owner.java`:**\n- `getFiscalYear()` \u2014 new getter returning `'FY<YY>'` from the business-day-adjusted registration date.\n- `getMembershipNumber()` \u2014 year segment now uses the fiscal year's `YY` (e.g. a 2026-09-18 registration now yields `-M27` instead of `-M26`, the behaviour change called out in the spec).\n- `getTenureDays()` \u2192 `getTenureFiscalYears()` \u2014 tenure is now elapsed fiscal years, not a 365-day window; `getMembershipPoints()` awards its tenure points once the owner has crossed at least one fiscal-year boundary.\n- Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`openapi.yml`:** added the `fiscalYear` read-only property (so it's generated into `OwnerDto` and auto-mapped by MapStruct), and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to match the new fiscal-year semantics.\n\nThe audit log confirms the end-to-end path: `registrationDate=2026-09-18 ... membershipNumber=NSW-...-M27`, and `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsFiscalYear` (asserting `fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) passes \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
